<title>USA: RJR Nabisco tobacco, food sales fell in Q1.</title>
<headline>RJR Nabisco tobacco, food sales fell in Q1.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-04-22</dateline>
<text>
<p>RJR Nabisco Holdings Corp said Tuesday first quarter sales were hurt by disruptions in tobacco exports from the former Soviet Union and the short-term impact of a sales force reorganization in the U.S. biscuit business.</p>
<p>For the first quarter, worldwide tobacco sales fell one percent from a year ago to $1.87 billion on a volume decline of nine percent.</p>
<p>International tobacco sales fell five percent to $798 million and volume fell 11 percent.</p>
</text>
